# MinURL manual API requests for local debugging.
# Recommended extension: VS Code REST Client (humao.rest-client).
#
# Quick start:
# 1) Start server: go run ./cmd/minurl
# 2) Execute requests top-to-bottom.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8888
@sampleOriginalURL = https://github.com/min0625

### Create short URL
# @name createShortURL
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/urls HTTP/1.1
content-type: application/json

{
  "original_url": "{{sampleOriginalURL}}"
}

### Create short URL with optional custom ID
# @name createShortURLWithCustomID
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/urls HTTP/1.1
content-type: application/json

{
  "original_url": "{{sampleOriginalURL}}",
  "id": "Min"
}

### Get short URL by ID (from create response)
# If create request has not been executed yet, run the create request first.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/urls/{{createShortURL.response.body.$.id}} HTTP/1.1

### Redirect to original URL (HTTP 302)
# Navigate to short URL to perform redirect to original URL
# If create request has not been executed yet, run the create request first.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/urls/{{createShortURL.response.body.$.id}}:redirect HTTP/1.1

### Redirect to original URL with custom ID (HTTP 302)
# Using the custom ID from createShortURLWithCustomID request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/urls/Min:redirect HTTP/1.1

### Not found example (expected HTTP 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/urls/NOT_FOUND_EXAMPLE HTTP/1.1

### Redirect not found example (expected HTTP 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/urls/NOT_FOUND_EXAMPLE:redirect HTTP/1.1
